 results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-4x+1 \\\\ (-7) & =-4(2)+1 \\\\ -7 & =-7\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498703 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0944b8cd-a8ad-5881-872d-cc7841b124b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498663} {:answer/id #uuid "0a037906-7560-5a7f-af3a-df39ea31c7f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498664} {:answer/id #uuid "2e04fce8-d81f-5c10-9a2d-ce00e7cc6157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498674} {:answer/id #uuid "64c6d466-8db0-5469-a154-b446a630e557" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498685} {:answer/id #uuid "cb659afb-f587-5d6a-8397-672e2e9f924f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0944b8cd-a8ad-5881-872d-cc7841b124b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498663} :answer-field/id #uuid "9124fd28-3c96-58aa-a8b1-46f977a63903" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498694}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b0bb51db-df3a-5c24-9053-c8f5081141e9" :question/problem "![](images/1a/1aa0849898f763eedd84d050a7bd7c24bbb10c8f89c81e3f533622252330814e.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=3x+4.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,-5)$, $B(1,5)$ and $C(2,10).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,-5)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (-5) & =3(-3)+4 \\\\ -5 & =-5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,5)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (5) & =3(1)+4 \\\\ 5 & =7\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,10)$ results in true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x+4 \\\\ (10) & =3(2)+4 \\\\ 10 & =10\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498706 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32181eed-9458-5ccf-acc4-92033b733168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498675} {:answer/id #uuid "6485fbd6-7602-59e9-b7db-664adfdbcd5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498684} {:answer/id #uuid "a768ab80-55c6-5d51-80fc-ee9ca1c3c7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498699} {:answer/id #uuid "b31cf4f4-e928-5d0a-810e-cf15a16aed3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498704} {:answer/id #uuid "ea9fccde-11ea-51fa-a5a6-450785e2da15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498713}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a768ab80-55c6-5d51-80fc-ee9ca1c3c7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498699} :answer-field/id #uuid "84d72100-1cce-5a74-8205-dd9bc89e56ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498692}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bbacf92b-66e8-58cd-bc32-e7d565177fbf" :question/problem "![](images/1f/1ff37e7ea63a62de2a1ccbf59c53225b739be305f9e87f7aceca7735ba210bbd.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-3x?$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-2,8),B(0,-2)$ and $C(2,-6).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-2,8)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x \\\\ (8) & =-3(-2)+0 \\\\ 8 & =6\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does *not* lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(0,-2)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x \\\\ (-2) & =-3(0)+0 \\\\ -2 & =0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,-6)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x \\\\ (-6) & =-3(2)+0 \\\\ -6 & =-6\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Points That Lie on a Line"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059716 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059530 :question/id #uuid "65198cdd-dd3b-5840-aaf3-cecd96eb9d3b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4301" :question/problem "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + 2b}{\\mid a + 2b \\mid}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na + 2b &= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + 2 \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 + 2 \\\\ 0 + (-2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid a + 2b \\mid &= \\sqrt{0^{2} + (-2)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4} \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + 2b}{\\mid a + 2b \\mid} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(a + 2b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c45a70b-273c-5fec-a768-40a1cf218628" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049360 :topic/math-academy-id 1104 :topic/title "Unit Vectors"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060119 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c0ae1f8-a9cf-50fb-bb0e-5bc2b25f22d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057073} {:answer/id #uuid "cc509d88-beba-52ad-90e8-932e39775b94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057074} {:answer/id #uuid "04113066-ce59-5327-a2a0-17fd031b7844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057075} {:answer/id #uuid "3b79648f-cdfe-5e7d-ab62-272eea15302a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057076} {:answer/id #uuid "5d6a7c46-b482-51be-a70e-62fa54b28535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057077}] :answer-field/id #uuid "278a8f50-693e-592e-9524-cda537320d44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057072}] :question/id #uuid "7fcb46f7-1c4e-5d49-b783-5c8f11cf4f94" :question/math-academy-id "q-17709" :question/problem "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a + 3b$ and points the same direction."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060129 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b3339c8-cfee-5d1c-ad46-ab44efd7b6e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{73}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{73}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057133} {:answer/id #uuid "96688b3e-d471-54f6-8aec-c73d555b7226" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{77}} \\\\ \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{77}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057134} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e8a09e-3906-503f-9e9f-3e6c5b353823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{73}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{73}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057135} {:answer/id #uuid "29a80b65-88dd-51a4-baa0-c738950c1264" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{73}} \\\\ \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{73}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057136} {:answer/id #uuid "401e5f5b-5db4-522a-9b7a-11b15f373032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{76}} \\\\ \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{76}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057137}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f8820177-fcee-5d33-9928-79e84e800cd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186057132}] :question/id #uuid "bfe76e58-e39f-55e9-9d8c-8f6cb0fc0443" :question/math-academy-id "q-18058" :question/problem "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a$ and points the same direction."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233367 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0602d7a4-2911-50a7-8931-1b4bc528c19a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{10}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411685} {:answer/id #uuid "3c5b6bc3-0505-592d-8bbe-21764c037dd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411711} {:answer/id #uuid "74dbb49a-6f69-59c5-ab9c-6bf2f84350df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411739} {:answer/id #uuid "8c50ba8e-c157-5ca3-9288-576321916d2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411752} {:answer/id #uuid "dda19a54-ac15-5715-b0ab-0a3f1c4ff8ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{10}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74dbb49a-6f69-59c5-ab9c-6bf2f84350df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411739} :answer-field/id #uuid "760bc6eb-d6bd-5bc8-a1ad-d57d71d59023" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411832}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eff15426-c7b2-53a2-8441-6bacd0c6dc45" :question/math-academy-id "q-125135" :question/problem "Let $b=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $b$ and points the same direction." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{b}{|\\,b\\,|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,b\\,| & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{b}{|b|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233368 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "06094a0c-ab74-504d-9e7a-29ff1a469a1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-125138" :question/problem "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $2a+b$ and points the same direction." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+b & =2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0+5 \\\\ 4+8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|2a+b| & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{12}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{169} \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $2a+b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}(2a+b) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{13} \\\\ \\frac{12}{13}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234271 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af9476c9-5aa2-526b-87d4-a82f7e7eeb39" :question/math-academy-id "q-70409" :question/problem "Let $n=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $n$ and points the same direction." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{n}{|\\,n\\,|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|n| & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{41}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $n$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{n}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{41}}\\cdot n \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{41}}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{41}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{41}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501424 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20917d48-ba12-5d1f-b21a-0ff1206db43b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2 \\sqrt{85}}{85} \\\\ \\frac{9 \\sqrt{85}}{85}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501420} {:answer/id #uuid "4448f5e2-51c2-5573-af62-a5a77921a60f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2 \\sqrt{85}}{85} \\\\ \\frac{3 \\sqrt{85}}{85}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501426} {:answer/id #uuid "69c38540-0ec4-5bc4-9f17-e6d71b15d3c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501431} {:answer/id #uuid "6d3a56cd-220c-5797-bf5d-1232e4735202" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2 \\sqrt{85}}{85} \\\\ - \\frac{9 \\sqrt{85}}{85}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501432} {:answer/id #uuid "bbfe8e76-81fa-5a5d-bd36-45854289df62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{85}}{85} \\\\ \\frac{9 \\sqrt{85}}{85}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20917d48-ba12-5d1f-b21a-0ff1206db43b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2 \\sqrt{85}}{85} \\\\ \\frac{9 \\sqrt{85}}{85}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501420} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca99c9f4-3bb7-5fbd-9bf4-f8cd3f0a0232" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501447}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3fe77d7b-c249-5da3-ae37-3fb1cc69e4ca" :question/problem "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $2a+b$ and points the same direction." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2a+b &= 2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0+(2) \\\\ (-4)+(13)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|2a+b| &= \\sqrt{(2)^2+(9)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{85} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{85}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $2a+b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{85}}\\cdot (2a+b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{85}}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2 \\sqrt{85}}{85} \\\\ \\frac{9 \\sqrt{85}}{85}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501425 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36b5a9a2-dc90-5731-af84-a45f4751626a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{20}{29} \\\\ \\frac{21}{29}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501422} {:answer/id #uuid "5d3cacb0-979d-5cd5-8d2c-9ce9ba39d324" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{10}{29} \\\\ - \\frac{21}{29}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501429} {:answer/id #uuid "7d5bb797-4d29-566d-8a17-e90b3639c09b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501434} {:answer/id #uuid "adcc82ff-26bb-5dc4-b727-5883ed507729" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{20}{29} \\\\ - \\frac{7}{29}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501440} {:answer/id #uuid "af4f327a-bbbc-5d9e-adf3-279321fc88a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{20}{29} \\\\ - \\frac{21}{29}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af4f327a-bbbc-5d9e-adf3-279321fc88a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{20}{29} \\\\ - \\frac{21}{29}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501442} :answer-field/id #uuid "075f845c-a443-544d-908f-2d88965db5a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501416}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "41db4b75-2005-5439-8a2f-cb0d807696ee" :question/problem "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $2a+b$ and points the same direction." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2a+b &= 2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0+(20) \\\\ (-4)+(-17)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -21\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|2a+b| &= \\sqrt{(20)^2+(-21)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{841} \\\\\n&= 29\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $2a+b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{29}\\cdot (2a+b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{29}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -21\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{20}{29} \\\\ - \\frac{21}{29}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501435 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17390a50-909e-519b-b1c9-2fd6e74d5286" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4 \\sqrt{65}}{65} \\\\ - \\frac{7 \\sqrt{65}}{65}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501419} {:answer/id #uuid "24652883-4d03-5d3a-94a2-7578f505b356" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501421} {:answer/id #uuid "3e7113a7-4e6f-50a3-ba67-bda8e88e5ac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4 \\sqrt{65}}{65} \\\\ \\frac{7 \\sqrt{65}}{65}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501423} {:answer/id #uuid "b19bb3ae-14c7-59ef-85c7-6d21c84a18fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4 \\sqrt{65}}{65} \\\\ - \\frac{7 \\sqrt{65}}{195}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501443} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b9b920-4cc5-5a82-a0bb-b0280d83ae64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2 \\sqrt{65}}{65} \\\\ - \\frac{7 \\sqrt{65}}{65}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17390a50-909e-519b-b1c9-2fd6e74d5286" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4 \\sqrt{65}}{65} \\\\ - \\frac{7 \\sqrt{65}}{65}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501419} :answer-field/id #uuid "af1f73f3-416d-515c-8b21-fd9ed0345370" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501441}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8567289b-a7cd-523c-8ba0-cb8ef5847d98" :question/problem "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $2a+b$ and points the same direction." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2a+b &= 2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0+(4) \\\\ (-6)+(-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|2a+b| &= \\sqrt{(4)^2+(-7)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{65} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{65}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $2a+b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{65}}\\cdot (2a+b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{65}}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4 \\sqrt{65}}{65} \\\\ - \\frac{7 \\sqrt{65}}{65}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501436 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f4424df-2c27-57d6-b91a-4c769aa3a3d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501417} {:answer/id #uuid "99a9035c-621d-5f0a-90b1-430b6da30043" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{12}{13} \\\\ - \\frac{5}{13}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501438} {:answer/id #uuid "9fcb7f83-60ae-5fd7-8845-026488417b53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{6}{13} \\\\ - \\frac{5}{13}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501439} {:answer/id #uuid "f1867dff-0f88-5922-972b-2e006c5e6a9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{12}{13} \\\\ - \\frac{5}{39}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501448} {:answer/id #uuid "f5b575f3-1801-524b-a76d-306e898a95d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{12}{13} \\\\ \\frac{5}{13}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501449}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99a9035c-621d-5f0a-90b1-430b6da30043" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{12}{13} \\\\ - \\frac{5}{13}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501438} :answer-field/id #uuid "45c48596-27ed-55c4-8123-7a3960c5a2e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501428}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "87c53303-b5c9-58af-aa9e-4eabf0ef314d" :question/problem "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $2a+b$ and points the same direction." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2a+b &= 2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0+(-12) \\\\ (-2)+(-3)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|2a+b| &= \\sqrt{(-12)^2+(-5)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{169} \\\\\n&= 13\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $2a+b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{13}\\cdot (2a+b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{13}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{12}{13} \\\\ - \\frac{5}{13}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501437 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "135f6880-f2d4-57f4-b6c2-f57d76de9846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{41} \\\\ \\frac{40}{123}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501418} {:answer/id #uuid "64d9579b-9034-5d26-9564-05a7d8dfa32d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501430} {:answer/id #uuid "71a98ba4-87aa-5cfb-85c6-16c3b6494b24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{41} \\\\ - \\frac{40}{41}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501433} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8348aa-d847-507f-b28b-29a3f3e30499" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{82} \\\\ \\frac{40}{41}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501445} {:answer/id #uuid "c52d8eab-2ff9-5a8e-b72b-8b924b645da0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{41} \\\\ \\frac{40}{41}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c52d8eab-2ff9-5a8e-b72b-8b924b645da0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{41} \\\\ \\frac{40}{41}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501446} :answer-field/id #uuid "449fcc00-8553-5455-8f81-e7253900c6b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501427}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9375cd18-2a95-552f-b85a-1ce8d0584d8e" :question/problem "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 38\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $2a+b$ and points the same direction." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2a+b &= 2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 38\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 38\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0+(9) \\\\ (2)+(38)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|2a+b| &= \\sqrt{(9)^2+(40)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{1681} \\\\\n&= 41\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $2a+b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{41}\\cdot (2a+b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{41}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{41} \\\\ \\frac{40}{41}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059730 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059543 :question/id #uuid "1ab8245a-39fb-5633-b5ff-865ab17dbfb9" :question/math-academy-id "e-4323" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 0,-0.4,11 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 2,5,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "Summing up the products of corresponding components, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =0\\cdot 2+(-0.4)\\cdot 5+11\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =0-2+22 \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68abb4f0-c532-5cb6-882c-dacfe6a945dc" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050173 :topic/math-academy-id 1166 :topic/title "Three-Dimensional Vectors in Component Form"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060030 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0888ddef-8bdd-5f2a-9651-377e2d59b4fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266221} {:answer/id #uuid "65cbccca-5647-533f-9957-61401f6703fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267047} {:answer/id #uuid "73c31d02-3131-57b8-a4b6-76ae1cf00f68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "39" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267162} {:answer/id #uuid "93171610-1482-5b05-a8ec-52bcb035bb11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267460} {:answer/id #uuid "bb720482-33b